455	648	Early life and education
Born at Bad Kreuznach in Rhineland-Palatinate, Verheugen studied history, sociology and political science at the University of Cologne and at the University of Bonn.



648	830	Political career
Verheugen was Secretary General of the Free Democratic Party of Germany (FDP) from 1978 to 1982, under the leadership of the party's chairman Hans-Dietrich Genscher.
831	958	He left the FDP with many left liberal party members in 1982, because the FDP left the government of Chancellor Helmut Schmidt.
959	1035	In the same year, he joined the Social Democratic Party of Germany (SPD).



